### 5. Reproduce Table 2 1-node and 7-node bench (cold-NEFF developer-faithful, v6)

We use `_v6` (and `_v7` for FSDP+PP, with N_LAYERS=4) which set
`WARMUP=0`, `N_ITER=3`, and report `warm_med` of the iterations after
the cold first-iter. This is the cold-NEFF developer-faithful methodology
(no warmup amortisation hiding compile cost).

1-node bench:

```bash
for prob in tp_mlp llama_block_ar a2av ua2a ring_kv; do
  torchrun --nproc_per_node=32 --nnodes=1 \
      experiments/h7_bench/bench_${prob}_v6.py
done
# FSDP and PP use v7 with N_LAYERS=4 for amplified per-call overhead:
for prob in fsdp_prefetch pp_send_recv; do
  torchrun --nproc_per_node=32 --nnodes=1 \
      experiments/h7_bench/bench_${prob}_v7.py
done
```

7-node bench: same scripts, `--nnodes=7 --rdzv_backend=static`:

```bash
torchrun --nproc_per_node=32 --nnodes=7 \
    --rdzv_backend=static --master_addr=$MASTER --master_port=29500 \
    experiments/h7_bench/bench_${prob}_v6.py
```

**Cross-scope inversion summary**: TP MLP and Layer-block AR show
baseline-faster (warm) across all stacks and scopes (the cleanest
demonstration). FSDP/PP/a2av/ua2a show baseline-faster in most
cells with 1-2 outliers per primitive. Ring KV is the **one exception**:
agent's per-slot AG (1 NEFF) beats baseline's per-head AG (32 NEFFs)
in every regime (warm and cold), because the 32:1 dispatch reduction
dominates over any compile cost.

### 6. Reproduce ablation tables (paper §7)

**Phase-3 ablation** (cc-react, multi-island; Tables 7, 8, 9): run
the search loop in step 1 with `--phase3-style cc-react` and
`--phase3-style multi-island`, then re-deploy and re-measure the
Table 3 / Table 6 commands above with the deployed runtimes from
each style. Per-style cost: ~$22 (cc-react), ~$24 (multi-island).

**No-simulator ablation** (paper §7.2, Table tab:ablation-nosim):
add `--no-simulator` to the search command in step 1 to skip
simulator-guided refinement (the agent picks the first
correct-and-HW-valid enumerated candidate without using
simulator-derived cost scores). Deploy the resulting runtimes and
re-run Table 3 OLMoE end-to-end (step 2) to see the
**0.75× regression** (5836 ms vs 4396 ms baseline) — the simulator
is necessary on 6/8 problems.

```bash
# No-sim search (writes runtime/trainium_*.py without simulator guidance)
python3 experiments/run_search.py \
    --problem alltoallv --phase3-style strategy-enumerate --no-simulator \
    --llm-model sonnet --max-rounds 4 --num-nodes 7 \
    --master-addr $MASTER --worker-addrs $WORKERS \
    --output-dir results/nosim/alltoallv
# ... repeat for the other 7 problems ...
```

### 7. Reproduce Figure 3 (cross-scope inversion diagram)

After Tables 2 + 6 data is collected:

```bash
python3 figures/gen_paper_figures.py  # writes figures/disagreement.pdf
```

### Late-phase probe methodology

We added two envvars to every training script: `PROBE_START_STEP` and
`PROBE_END_STEP`. Per-call `.item()` probes inside autograd
`Function.forward/backward` are skipped until step ≥ `PROBE_START_STEP`
and disabled again after `PROBE_END_STEP`. This avoids the host syncs
that contaminate steady-state and skips the early NEFF-compile transient
where per-step time is non-stationary.

For the **per-problem training scripts** (small models, single primitive
under test) late-phase `.item()` probes succeed and give accurate
per-call latency at training scope — these are the values populating
Table 2's `7n-training` column. For the **OLMoE-10B 7-node end-to-end
script** (`training/train_olmoe10b.py`) `.item()` probes still hit
Neuron HBM limits even with late-phase gating, so we revert to
`xm.add_step_closure(...)` for the per-call timing (silent / less
precise but consistent). This is why the AllToAllV / dxe
training-scope cells in Table 2 are from the OLMoE
`add_step_closure` probe while the TP MLP / FSDP / Layer-block AR /
PP cross-stage cells are from the per-problem `.item()` probes.

## Per-Problem Training-Scope Cost (Table 2 summary)

Per-call training-scope cost across the eight Llama-side and
OLMoE-side per-problem training scripts (median over the three
search-style runs, 7-node 224-rank):

| Problem          | Baseline / call | Agent / call           | Win  |
|------------------|----------------:|-----------------------:|-----:|
| TP MLP           |        34.19 ms | 33.00 ms               |  ~3% |
| FSDP prefetch    |        36.22 ms | 30.6–31.3 ms           | ~14% |
| Layer-block AR   |        53.37 ms | 44.7–45.8 ms           | ~15% |
| AllToAllV (OLMoE) |      126.60 ms | 91.2–91.5 ms           | ~28% |
| dxe              |        13.50 ms | 11.64–14.20 ms         | 3–15% |
| PP cross-stage   |          8.11 ms |  3.73–3.80 ms          | ~2× |

Notes:
- The bundled compositions win at the per-step layer once each
  per-call latency is multiplied by the corresponding calls-per-step
  (M=4 for the per_mb path on the four Llama-side primitives, 1 for
  the bundled path).

## 7-Node OLMoE-Style End-to-End Comparison

A single MoE training loop that exercises **two** of the searched
collectives simultaneously — AllToAllV and distributed cross-entropy —
inside `training/train_olmoe10b.py`, run on **7× trn1.32xlarge
(224 ranks)**.

Architecture: **OLMoE-architectural-style** (no MLA, no shared experts,
standard multi-head attention + RoPE + RMSNorm + SwiGLU MoE) with
**expert-choice routing** so per-(src,dst) send/receive counts are
fixed at `cap` tokens each. With `NEXP = ws = 224` (one expert per rank)
the AllToAllV call becomes a uniform-shape exchange with no per-step
host-side count computation.

| | |
|---|---|
| LAYERS | 8 |
| DM | 2048 |
| HEADS | 16 |
| NEXP | 224 (1 expert per rank, expert-choice routing) |
| TOPK | 8 (average expert calls per token) |
| EXDIM | 1024 |
| SEQLEN | 256, BSZ=1, bf16 |
| VOCAB | 32256 (= 224 · 144, sharded across ranks for dxe) |
| cap | `ceil(SEQLEN · TOPK / NEXP) · 1.0 = 10` tokens per (src expert, dst rank) |
| Total params | ~10 B at world=224 (replicated 197 M, expert ~44 M × 224) |

Two independently pluggable collective backends — each can be
`baseline` (developer-written reference) or `agent` (the 7-node search
output in `runtime/trainium_*_7node.py`):

| Collective | Baseline | Agent |
|---|---|---|
| AllToAllV (MoE dispatch + combine) | AG + reshape + RS-SUM | pack + 1 `all_gather` + `index_select` (`runtime/trainium_alltoallv_7node.py`) |
| Distributed cross-entropy | `all_gather` full logits + `F.cross_entropy` | 2 `all_reduce`s, no max-shift, bf16-safe (`runtime/trainium_dxe_7node.py`) |

